{"term":"identify","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b3cd9afd7a15a8b26f","definition":"To establish the identity of someone or something.","example":"It was hard to identify the shoplifter because the CCTV records didn't have a clear image.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eca33ef316f9080381","definition":"To disclose the identity of someone.","example":"The Associated Press will not identify the suspect of the crime because he is a juvenile.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f6e4d37510014bbd4","definition":"To establish the taxonomic classification of an organism.","example":"A recent biological inventory uncovered 41 species and 2 subspecies of insects new to science and many species not before identified in the State of Washington.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f6f538bbc79ad2e99d","definition":"To equate or make the same; to unite or combine into one.","example":"Every precaution is taken to identify the interests of the people, and their rulers.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4f5cd81db0c806c739","definition":"To have a strong affinity with; to feel oneself to be modelled on or connected to.","example":"Der Traum erhält eine neue Deutung, wenn sie im Traum nicht sich, sondern die Freundin meint, wenn sie sich an die Stelle der Freundin gesetzt oder, wie wir sagen können, sich mit ihr identifiziert hat.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive","register":"reflexive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eec154da8f1be3077b","definition":"To associate oneself with some group; to feel, or believe one feels, the same way.","example":"Now, the vast majority of us identify with the second group, the one that believes in trusting the wisdom of the people rather than taking power away from them and concentrating it in the other hands.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:12eeacaf24d5df5bbf","definition":"To claim an identity; to describe oneself as a member of a group; to assert the use of a particular term to describe oneself.","example":"\"The main message is that it's the interface between individuals and society that causes students who identify as gay, lesbian, or bisexual the most distress,\" said study first author Yue Zhao.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["ID","clock","identify","ken","to make someone","notice","recognize","twig"],"antonyms":["misken"],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive","register":"reflexive","wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/identify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/aɪˈdɛn.tɪ.faɪ/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a7/En-us-identify.ogg/En-us-identify.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["deidentify","disidentify","hyperidentify","identifiability","identifiable","identifiee","identifier","identifyee","misidentify","nonidentified","nonidentifying","overidentify","photoidentify","preidentified","reidentify","self-identify","underidentified","unidentified","unidentifying"]}